POWI is a fab-lite semiconductor company, relying on foundries for manufacturing, which introduces dependency risks. The company faces cyclical demand in data center and consumer markets, with limited visibility on inventory digestion. Its customer concentration in these end-markets exposes it to capex cycle volatility.  

